The rules are reimplementations written for codelaw. Their `ported_from:`
fields name the ESLint rules (https://eslint.org, MIT License) whose documented
behaviour they reproduce; no ESLint code or documentation text is included.

The `js/promise-*` rules reproduce the documented behaviour of
eslint-plugin-promise 7.3.0 (https://github.com/eslint-community/eslint-plugin-promise,
ISC License); no code or documentation text of it is included.

The rules whose `ported_from:` names a `biome/` rule reproduce the documented
behaviour of Biome 2.6.4 (https://biomejs.dev, MIT License); no Biome code or
documentation text is included.

The `js/jsdoc-*` rules reproduce the documented behaviour of eslint-plugin-jsdoc
65.4.2 (https://github.com/gajus/eslint-plugin-jsdoc, BSD-3-Clause License);
the `js/import-*` rules that of eslint-plugin-import 2.32.0
(https://github.com/import-js/eslint-plugin-import, MIT License) and
eslint-plugin-import-x 4.17.1 (https://github.com/un-ts/eslint-plugin-import-x,
MIT License); the rules whose `ported_from:` names an `oxlint/` rule that of
Oxlint (https://oxc.rs, MIT License); and those naming a `tslint/` rule that of
TSLint (https://palantir.github.io/tslint/, Apache License 2.0). No code or
documentation text of any of them is included.
